 ## Changelog
 
+- 2026-10-26 (15): the flat satchel and a recipe book replace the pack's cloth screen (**NOT b1.7.3**; written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device; +6 tests in `world/book.rs`, +5 in `satchel.rs`, `options_txt_round_trips` extended; run `cargo test --lib book satchel options` first). Request of the player: the 3D table was too dizzying to use all the time; a bag for the inventory and a book of every recipe beside it, the book's left page the categories then the list, its right page the 2x2 grid. `Screen::click`, `SlotId`, `pack::layout` / `sort` and the vanilla panels (furnace, chests, the pack switch off) are untouched; the cloth, `Mat`, the camera glide and the tabs stay in `pack.rs` and run only with `packCloth:true`.
+    - Screen (`satchel.rs`): `Frame::new(sat, inv, gw, w, h)` is every rect in px (fractions of the height, text unit `craft::panel(0, w, h).2`), `Frame::hit` says what a finger is on (`Pick`), `draw` / `draw_pin` paint it; `lib.rs` only opens it (`open_satchel`: the inventory button, or a workbench with the book already open), routes the finger (`on_sat_tap`, `sat_pick`, a drag on the list scrolls, a press on the result held `HOLD_SECS` crafts all) and closes it (`close_screen` puts the grid and the held stack back in the bag first). `TouchUi::pack_open` is set while it is up (every press a tap, the four HUD buttons hidden), buttons: Book, Sort, Shift, One above the bag, X at the corner. The bag rises in 0.25 s, the book opens in 0.3 s (both pages grow from the spine), a category slides in in 0.2 s. The world behind is dimmed.
+    - Book closed: the bag with the cloth's zones (flat, scaled to fit). Book open: the bag slides to the left 45% and packs into 9 x 3 + the belt + the armor row (cells at least 8% of the height, checked by a test), so the thumb has room; every slot keeps its `SlotId`.
+    - Recipes (`world/book.rs`): `entries()` is every `craft::recipes()` entry (new accessors `Recipe::out` / `shape` / `pattern`, `craft::code` / `unpack` / `smelting` public) plus every smelting, in six `Cat`s; `craftable` / `missing` / `have` count the bag (main slots, the belt) and the grid; `fill` (a tap on a recipe) empties the grid into the bag, then takes one set of ingredients (main slots first, the belt last) into the recipe's own cells, and changes nothing when it fails (a 3x3 recipe at the 2x2 grid, something short, no room); `craft_all` is fill + `shift_click(Result)` in a loop until the bag runs dry or full; wool and dye match by colour (`craft::code`).
+    - Notes (`book::Notes`, `<world>/book`, 69 bytes `BK1` + pin + 64 bytes of seen item ids, written with the level): `observe` marks every id the bag or grid holds each frame; `known(entry)` = its result or any ingredient was held; with `bookDiscovery:true` (the toggle on the right page) an unknown recipe is a dark `?` box and `???`, is not filled, and its card says to find an item; off (the default) everything shows. Pin: one recipe's card (result, each ingredient with have / need, green / red) at the left of the play HUD (`draw_pin`).
+    - New: `packCloth` and `bookDiscovery` in `options.txt` (`Settings::pack_cloth`, `book_discovery`, default off).
+    - Not done, on purpose (ponytail): no blur behind the bag (dimmed); an unknown recipe is a dark box, not the item's silhouette (`push_stack` has no tint); list rows half out of the list are not drawn instead of clipped; the pin is an index into `entries()` (a later release that adds recipes can shift it: a pin past the list is dropped); no item physics or shadows in the flat bag, the items are the HUD icons; the furnace and chests keep their vanilla panels; furnace recipes are information only; the cloth code is not deleted yet (delete `Mat` and the camera glide once the satchel has been seen on a device).
+    - UNVERIFIED: all proportions (fractions of the height), the colours, the sound, and the touch feel of the list scroll and the 0.5 s hold; tune them on the phone.
+    - Rebased on the upstream with entry (14): the book reads `craft::recipes()`, so the new furnace-cart, chest-cart, compass and clock recipes are listed with no line more; the chest cart (342) joins the redstone & rails page with the other carts.
 - 2026-10-25 (14): furnace cart recipe, Nether compass / clock spin, Rename world (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +1 test `menu::tests::rename_changes_the_name_only`, +1 `anim::tests::the_nether_spins_both_hands`, +3 asserts in `craft::tests::recipes_match_like_java`).
     - `craft.rs`: the minecart with furnace is `shaped(["A","B"])` (furnace over minecart) as in `CraftingManager`; it was shapeless (any order, any cells).
     - `anim.rs` `Anim::gauges(.., nether)`: in the Nether both targets are `random * 2 pi` every tick (`TextureCompassFX.onTick`, `TextureWatchFX.onTick`: `worldProvider.isNether`), so needle and dial spin; `lib.rs` passes `self.nether`. The overworld path is unchanged. (The compass and clock already animated before this entry; entry (13)'s "Not done" line said they did not, which was wrong.)
